<title>INDIA: India SAIL down seven pct before results.</title>
<headline>India SAIL down seven pct before results.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Steel Authority of India (SAIL) fell 1.50 rupees, or 7.3 percent, to 19 rupees on the Bombay bourse on Wednesday ahead of the firm's results for 1996/97, traders said.  </p>
<p>The net profit of the country's largest steelmaker is likely to fall to 6.53 billion rupees, from 13.29 billion in 1995/96, the Economic Times newspaper said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The newspaper quoted unnamed company sources as saying that SAIL was likely to cut its 150 billion investments planned for the next five years due to increased competition and plunging profits.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
